WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.620
- So, before we close out the show,

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:04.100
I've got one last story
to give you all the feels.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:04.980
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.480
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.880
More than 25 years ago,

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.350
Jed was a high school
football player in Arizona

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:13.900
who earned his Letterman jacket.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.260
He designed it himself

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.150
and was all ready to
pick it up at the store

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.340
when his mom confessed,

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.440
she just didn't have
the money to pay for it.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:22.900
Jed understood and he
never got the jacket.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.130
That is, until the end of last year,

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:27.770
when it serendipitously
came back into his life.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.940
His tale is so amazing.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.710
We have Jed on the line
to explain it right now.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.002
What's up, Jed?

00:00:32.002 --> 00:00:33.752
(audience applauds)

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:35.390
- Howdy, thanks for having me.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.520
- Oh my god, this story is crazy.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.890
Tell everybody how you ended up

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:41.840
with your jacket after decades.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.280
- Well, back in high school,
I ordered a Letterman jacket.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.400
When it was time to pick it up,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.470
my mom couldn't afford it

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.790
and it wasn't that I was mad.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.740
It was just another speed
bump that I had to get over

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.230
during my rough childhood.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.540
We grew up with IOUs
under the Christmas tree

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.630
and my mother really had
trouble making ends meet.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:03.470
Now, she did the best job
that she possibly could

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:05.900
and gave us nothing but love.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.331
Fast forward to November of 2021.

00:01:09.331 --> 00:01:12.550
27 years later, my big brother, Josh,

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:13.960
who lives three and a half hours

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.480
outside of where we grew up,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:20.270
walks into a thrift store
and sees this jacket.

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.137
He calls me up and says,

00:01:21.137 --> 00:01:25.042
"Dude, was there any other
Jeds at Chaparral in 1994?"

00:01:25.042 --> 00:01:28.310
(Kelly laughs)
I said, "No," just one.

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:29.570
He sends me the picture.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:33.140
I knew immediately that
that was my jacket.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.580
He tells me that it was $25.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.190
I said, "Buy that right now,
I'm flying home to see you."

00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:39.023
- [Kelly] Oh my god.

00:01:39.023 --> 00:01:40.000
- When he put the jacket on me,

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.330
it was one of the
greatest days of my life.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.791
- That's so cool.

00:01:43.791 --> 00:01:45.000
(audience applauds)
Like, later on in life,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.660
I bet it has so much more meaning now

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:49.220
than it would have even had

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.550
if you would have gotten
it back in the day.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:51.950
That's so cool!

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.880
So deeper meaning, does it
have deeper meaning to you

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.130
than just getting the memento, right?

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.420
- Kelly, my mom was the most

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:01.440
religious person I've
ever come in contact with.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.790
We went to church every Sunday.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.220
She passed away back in 2012

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.510
and she told us that she would

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.670
always send us a sign from the other side.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:12.200
A couple of weeks before this happened,

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.100
I was just telling a friend
that that never happened.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.910
If this isn't a sign,
I don't know what is.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.000
And, you know, was this
divine intervention?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:21.833
I don't know.

00:02:21.833 --> 00:02:25.020
But what I do know, is that
it gives me faith in humanity

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.960
and hope that anything is possible.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:29.730
- I definitely think that's a sign, man.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.530
That's the coolest story.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.460
That's the coolest part,

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.210
that she told you that
she'd send you a sign

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.043
and then you ended up finding it.

00:02:35.043 --> 00:02:36.670
What are the chances of that happening?

00:02:36.670 --> 00:02:37.660
That's so cool.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:39.070
Well, thank you so much, Jed.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:41.480
I'm liking your post right now, right?

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.313
- [Jed] Awesome.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:44.930
- And that's not all, my man.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.930
Our season-long partner,
Pilot pen makers of G2,

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.010
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.530
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.950
So, they're going to be
writing you a check for $1000.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:58.480
How's that?
(audience cheers)

00:02:58.480 --> 00:02:59.562
- Thank you so much-

00:02:59.562 --> 00:03:02.148
- [Kelly] Absolutely! Absolutely, man.

